  "reason": "The current best is config_027 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250 acc. The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder, imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion. The one remaining untested variation within this top-performing neighborhood is the fusion method: config_017 tests scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat. This is the cleanest ablation of the best config, directly clarifying whether weighted fusion provides a meaningful advantage over concat in the strongest regime (prior comparisons suggest weighted > concat by ~2-3%, but those were with scgpt or avgpool). If concat performs comparably, the architecture is robust and we can focus remaining budget on confirming the best; if weighted is clearly better, we lock in config_027 as the final answer with high confidence. Expected cost is ~3.5–4 GPU hours (same architecture as config_027 at 3.60, only fusion layer changes), making it a low-cost, high-information experiment. With 3 experiments remaining after this, this targeted test maximizes the chance of either finding a marginal improvement or confidently confirming the optimum within budget."
}

